## Exit code with `--code-coverage`

A failing scope must give a failing exit code even when it is not the last
scope that runs.

```catala
declaration scope Fails:
  output x content integer

scope Fails:
  definition x equals 1
  assertion x = 2

declaration scope Passes:
  output y content integer

scope Passes:
  definition y equals 1
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala interpret --code-coverage -s Fails -s Passes
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Assertion failed: 1 ≠ 2
│
├─➤ tests/assertions/bad/coverage_exit_code.catala_en:12.3-18:
│    │
│ 12 │   assertion x = 2
│    │   ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Exit code with `--code-coverage`
┌─[RESULT]─ Passes ─
│ y = 1
└─
#return code 123#
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala interpret -s Fails -s Passes
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Assertion failed: 1 ≠ 2
│
├─➤ tests/assertions/bad/coverage_exit_code.catala_en:12.3-18:
│    │
│ 12 │   assertion x = 2
│    │   ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Exit code with `--code-coverage`
┌─[RESULT]─ Passes ─
│ y = 1
└─
#return code 123#
```
